WEBVTT

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:05.374
With thirty-three elements and thirty-two
threads per block, main launches two

00:00:05.374 --> 00:00:05.846
blocks.

00:00:06.026 --> 00:00:10.228
Each thread needs to work out which array
index belongs to it.

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:14.615
CUDA grid of one returns the index across
all blocks.

00:00:14.795 --> 00:00:18.905
Multiply the block number by the threads
per block and add the thread number.

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:22.835
Block one, thread zero gets index
thirty-two.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.855
Index thirty-two is the last valid
position.

00:00:27.035 --> 00:00:31.052
The next thread gets thirty-three and skips
the reads and write.

00:00:31.232 --> 00:00:36.903
Put both indices into the kernel's bounds
check to see which thread enters the if

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:37.281
block.

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:42.601
In main, change the launch to three blocks
of sixteen threads each.

00:00:42.781 --> 00:00:46.345
Block two, thread zero writes the same
array position.

00:00:46.525 --> 00:00:51.912
The diagnostic print in the notebook shows
that thread's block and thread numbers.
